---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro"

// Keep this in step with what the site actually loads: BaseLayout (analytics), Comments (Disqus),
// AudioPlayer (local storage) and any embeds in posts.
const updated = "October 21, 2026"
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How shaunpezeshki.com handles your information: what's collected, which services are involved, and your choices."
  keywords="Privacy policy, Shaun Pezeshki, Google Analytics, Disqus, Cloudflare"
>
  <section class="page-head" data-reveal-group>
    <div class="shell">
      <h1 data-reveal>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="page-head__lede" data-reveal>Last updated {updated}.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="shell page-body">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This is my personal website. I don't sell your information, and there are no ads or accounts here. A few
        outside services help count visits, run comments and play embedded media. Each one is listed below.
      </p>

      <h2>What I collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Visits.</strong> Google Analytics records which pages are viewed, roughly where visitors are, and what
          device and browser they use. It sets cookies to do this. If your browser sends a Do Not Track signal, Google
          Analytics doesn't load on this site at all.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Emails you send me.</strong> If you email me, I keep your message and address so I can reply.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Comments.</strong> Comments on stories are run by Disqus. Anything you post there, and the cookies
          Disqus sets, are covered by its own privacy policy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <p>
        The audio player remembers where you stopped in each story and the speed you like. That's saved in your own
        browser and never sent to me. Clearing your browser data removes it.
      </p>

      <h2>Services this site uses</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site. Like any host, it handles basic request data such as IP addresses
          to deliver pages and block abuse.{" "}
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics</strong> counts visits, as described above.{" "}
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Disqus</strong> runs comments and only loads when you scroll near them.{" "}
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://help.disqus.com/en/articles/1717103-disqus-privacy-policy">Disqus's policy</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>TikTok</strong> loads its player on the one story that embeds a TikTok video.{" "}
          <a target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" href="https://www.tiktok.com/legal/privacy-policy-us">TikTok's policy</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Links to Calendly, Buy Me a Coffee, LinkedIn, Instagram and X take you to those sites, where their own policies
        apply.
      </p>

      <h2>How I use information</h2>
      <p>
        Only to run this site, see which stories people read, and reply to messages. I don't sell or rent personal
        information, and I don't share it beyond the services listed above.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Turn on Do Not Track in your browser to stop Google Analytics here.</li>
        <li>Block or clear cookies in your browser settings.</li>
        <li>Email me to ask what I have about you, or to have it deleted.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>California privacy rights</h2>
      <p>If you live in California, the CCPA lets you ask me to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Tell you what personal information I've collected about you.</li>
        <li>Delete the personal information I've collected about you.</li>
        <li>Not sell your personal information. I don't sell it, but you can still ask.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To make a request, email <a href="mailto:shaun@uphighstudio.com">shaun@uphighstudio.com</a>. I'll respond
        within 45 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This site isn't meant for children under 13, and I don't knowingly collect their information.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, I'll update this page and the date at the top.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy? Email <a href="mailto:shaun@uphighstudio.com">shaun@uphighstudio.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
